layer_library.py, tests/test_cli_contract.py, README.md | 2026-07-16T18:49:45Z |\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/AudioExplainer/coord/BOARD.md:37:| T-007 | Add continuous article transcript view and publish AudioExplainer | codex | claude | none | 2026-07-11T15:48:58Z |\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/AudioExplainer/coord/BOARD.md:40:| T-004 | Same-day HTML transcript-following player plan | codex | claude | coord/council/C-001-player-sync-same-day-plan/**, coord/work/codex/T-004-*, coord/threads/*T-004* | 2026-07-10T19:16:37Z |\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/AudioExplainer/coord/BOARD.md:43:| T-003 | Audio library + transcript-following design | codex | claude+agy | design only; per-project library, replay UX, sentence sync feasibility | 2026-07-10T02:45:20Z |\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/AudioExplainer/coord/work/agy/T-010-multimedia-research.md:26:   - Fuse ASR transcripts and OCR/VLM text from frames.\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/AudioExplainer/coord/work/agy/T-010-multimedia-research.md:45:- **Timestamp Alignment:** ASR text chunks may not perfectly align with the visual slide changes. **Mitigation:** Use fuzzy timestamp matching or windowed fusion (grouping transcript text by the time segment of the visible slide).\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/AudioExplainer/coord/work/codex/T-001-audio-explainer-rfc-notes.md:45:agent discovery: stdin in, MP3/transcript out, final stdout line is the MP3\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/AudioExplainer/coord/work/codex/T-001-audio-explainer-rfc-notes.md:157:include the final transcript next to the MP3. The manifest makes concat failures\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/AudioExplainer/coord/work/claude/T-001-audio-explainer-design.md:41:WPM duration estimate, `.md` transcript next to audio, MP3 to /tmp.\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/AudioExplainer/coord/work/claude/T-001-audio-explainer-design.md:42:What we keep: the engine, aliases, guard, transcript, duration estimate.\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/AudioExplainer/coord/work/claude/T-001-audio-explainer-design.md:60:  transcript; print the MP3 path on stdout; optional `--play` (afplay on macOS).\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/AudioExplainer/coord/work/claude/T-001-audio-explainer-design.md:140:- **CLI conformance contract (codex):** stdin in → MP3 + transcript out; final\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/AudioExplainer/coord/work/claude/T-001-audio-explainer-design.md:206:  transcript, CLI contract (final stdout = mp3 path).\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/AudioExplainer/coord/COLLAB_POLICY.md:170:The first-class message type is `type: dissent`. Legacy threads may contain\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/AudioExplainer/coord/council/C-001-player-sync-same-day-plan/question.md:1:# Council C-001: For AudioExplainer's existing self-contained HTML player, what exact same-day MVP should we implement to deliver sentence-following transcript playback and a useful per-output-directory library without overbuilding, while preserving offline behavior, provider fallbacks, CLI stdout compatibility, and the current dirty worktree? Specify UX, data/schema, provider boundary capture, file ownership/order, tests, explicit deferrals, and explain why plain text alone cannot provide interactive synchronized highlighting.\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/AudioExplainer/coord/council/C-001-player-sync-same-day-plan/question.md:11:For AudioExplainer's existing self-contained HTML player, what exact same-day MVP should we implement to deliver sentence-following transcript playback and a useful per-output-directory library without overbuilding, while preserving offline behavior, provider fallbacks, CLI stdout compatibility, and the current dirty worktree? Specify UX, data/schema, provider boundary capture, file ownership/order, tests, explicit deferrals, and explain why plain text alone cannot provide interactive synchronized highlighting.\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/AudioExplainer/coord/council/C-001-player-sync-same-day-plan/decision.md:31:A txt or Markdown file can store transcript text and even literal timecodes, but it cannot by itself follow playback. It has no audio currentTime, timeupdate or seek events, addressable sentence elements, active styling, auto-scroll, click-to-seek, or persistence. HTML plus JavaScript is the correct offline interaction layer. WebVTT could be a future timed-data export, but a clickable scrolling transcript still needs a consuming UI.\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/AudioExplainer/coord/council/C-001-player-sync-same-day-plan/decision.md:41:5. say and invalid/missing Edge metadata degrade honestly to the existing static transcript with no fake highlight.\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/AudioExplainer/coord/council/C-001-player-sync-same-day-plan/decision.md:48:Before enlarging the embedded payload, fix the current player serialization. Raw json.dumps inside a script can be terminated by transcript/title content containing </script>. Escape less-than, greater-than, ampersand, U+2028, and U+2029 to Unicode escapes; create all transcript DOM with textContent, never innerHTML; add a regression containing </script>. This is the first implementation slice.\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/AudioExplainer/coord/council/C-001-player-sync-same-day-plan/decision.md:64:- Use Edge's exact returned boundary text as the timed transcript; never reconstruct sentences from the Markdown artifact.\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/AudioExplainer/coord/council/C-001-player-sync-same-day-plan/decision.md:75:- audio, transcript, and player filenames\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/AudioExplainer/coord/council/C-001-player-sync-same-day-plan/decision.md:85:- transcript opens by default as a semantic sentence list;\nfrom manim import *\n\nclass NashEquilibriumWithAudio(Scene):\n    def construct(self):\n        # Configurar escena\n        self.camera.background_color = \"#1e1e1e\"  # Fondo oscuro profesional\n        \n        # Audio intro + título\n        self.add_sound(\"audio/intro.mp3\")\n        title = Text(\"Equilibrio de Nash\", font_size=54, color=BLUE_C, weight=BOLD)\n        subtitle = Text(\"Dilema del Prisionero\", font_size=40, color=GRAY_A)\n        title.to_edge(UP, buff=0.8)\n        subtitle.next_to(title, DOWN, buff=0.4)\n        \n        self.play(Write(title), run_time=2)\n        self.play(Write(subtitle), run_time=2)\n        self.wait(2)\n        \n        # Transición a explicación de jugadores\n        self.play(FadeOut(title), FadeOut(subtitle), run_time=1)\n        \n        # Audio explicación de jugadores\n        self.add_sound(\"audio/players.mp3\") \n        \n        # Configurar jugadores y estrategias\n        player1_label = Text(\"Jugador 1\", font_size=32, color=GREEN_C, weight=BOLD)\n        player1_label.move_to([-5, 2.5, 0])\n        \n        player2_label = Text(\"Jugador 2\", font_size=32, color=RED_C, weight=BOLD)\n        player2_label.move_to([2, 3.8, 0])\n        \n        cooperate_1 = Text(\"Cooperar\", font_size=24, color=GREEN_B).move_to([-5, 1.2, 0])\n        defect_1 = Text(\"Traicionar\", font_size=24, color=RED_B).move_to([-5, -0.8, 0])\n        \n        cooperate_2 = Text(\"Cooperar\", font_size=24, color=GREEN_B).move_to([0, 3.2, 0])\n        defect_2 = Text(\"Traicionar\", font_size=24, color=RED_B).move_to([3.5, 3.2, 0])\n        \n        # Mostrar jugadores y estrategias con timing\n        self.play(Write(player1_label), run_time=1.5)\n        self.play(Write(player2_label), run_time=1.5)\n        self.wait(1)\n        \n        self.play(Write(cooperate_1), Write(defect_1), run_time=2)\n        self.play(Write(cooperate_2), Write(defect_2), run_time=2)\n        self.wait(1)\n        \n        # Audio matriz de pagos\n        self.add_sound(\"audio/payoff_matrix.mp3\")\n        \n        # Crear tabla más atractiva\n        payoff_data = [\n            [\"(3,3)\", \"(0,5)\"],\n            [\"(5,0)\", \"(1,1)\"]\n        ]\n        \n        table = Table(\n            payoff_data,\n            row_labels=[Text(\"C\", font_size=24, color=GREEN_B), Text(\"T\", font_size=24, color=RED_B)],\n            col_labels=[Text(\"C\", font_size=24, color=GREEN_B), Text(\"T\", font_size=24, color=RED_B)],\n            include_outer_lines=True,\n            element_to_mobject=lambda x: Text(x, font_size=28, color=WHITE),\n            line_config={\"color\": BLUE_C, \"stroke_width\": 2}\n        ).move_to([1.8, 0.5, 0]).scale(0.9)\n        \n        # Animar creación de tabla\n        self.play(Create(table), run_time=3)\n        self.wait(3)\n        \n        # Audio equilibrio Nash\n        self.add_sound(\"audio/nash_explanation.mp3\")\n        \n        # Resaltar equilibrio de Nash con animación llamativa\n        nash_eq = table.get_entries_without_labels()[3]  # (1,1)\n        nash_highlight = SurroundingRectangle(\n            nash_eq, \n            color=YELLOW, \n            buff=0.15, \n            stroke_width=4\n        )\n        \n        # Pulso en el equilibrio\n        self.play(Create(nash_highlight), run_time=1)\n        self.play(nash_highlight.animate.scale(1.2), run_time=0.5)\n        self.play(nash_highlight.animate.scale(0.83), run_time=0.5)  # Regresa a tamaño normal\n        \n        nash_text = Text(\"Equilibrio de Nash\", font_size=28, color=YELLOW, weight=BOLD)\n        nash_arrow = Arrow(\n            start=nash_text.get_top() + UP*0.3,\n            end=nash_eq.get_center() + DOWN*0.8,\n            color=YELLOW,\n            stroke_width=3\n        )\n        nash_text.next_to(table, DOWN, buff=0.8)\n        \n        self.play(Write(nash_text), run_time=1.5)\n        self.play(Create(nash_arrow), run_time=1)\n        self.wait(2)\n        \n        # Audio resultado subóptimo\n        self.add_sound(\"audio/suboptimal.mp3\")\n        \n        # Resaltar resultado óptimo\n        optimal_eq = table.get_entries_without_labels()[0]  # (3,3)\n        optimal_highlight = SurroundingRectangle(\n            optimal_eq,\n            color=GREEN,\n            buff=0.15,\n            stroke_width=4\n        )\n        \n        optimal_text = Text(\"Resultado Óptimo\", font_size=24, color=GREEN, weight=BOLD)\n        optimal_text.next_to(nash_text, DOWN, buff=0.5)\n        \n        self.play(Create(optimal_highlight), run_time=1)\n        self.play(Write(optimal_text), run_time=1.5)\n        self.wait(2)\n        \n        # Comparación visual\n        comparison = VGroup(\n            Text(\"Nash: (1,1) - Subóptimo\", font_size=22, color=RED),\n            Text(\"Óptimo: (3,3) - Cooperación\", font_size=22, color=GREEN)\n        ).arrange(DOWN, aligned_edge=LEFT, buff=0.3)\n        comparison.next_to(optimal_text, DOWN, buff=0.8)\n        \n        self.play(Write(comparison), run_time=3)\n        self.wait(3)\n        \n        # Audio conclusión\n        self.add_sound(\"audio/conclusion.mp3\")\n        \n        # Transición a mensaje final\n        all_objects = VGroup(\n            player1_label, player2_label,\n            cooperate_1, defect_1, cooperate_2, defect_2,\n            table, nash_highlight, optimal_highlight,\n            nash_text, nash_arrow, optimal_text, comparison\n        )\n        \n        self.play(FadeOut(all_objects), run_time=2)\n        \n        # Mensaje final con estilo\n        final_title = Text(\"¡Equilibrio de Nash!\", font_size=48, color=BLUE_C, weight=BOLD)\n        final_subtitle = Text(\"Racionalidad individual ≠ Resultado óptimo\", font_size=32, color=WHITE)\n        \n        final_group = VGroup(final_title, final_subtitle).arrange(DOWN, buff=0.5)\n        \n        self.play(Write(final_title), run_time=2)\n        self.play(Write(final_subtitle), run_time=2)\n        self.wait(3)/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/econ100a-slides_homeworks/docs/S5_Choice_Ch5.md:56:* Suppose that only thing you know is that your MRS, at the bundle $ (x_1', x_2') $, is higher in magnitude than $ p_1 / p_2$. That is, the associated indifference curve is steeper than the budget constraint.\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/econ100a-slides_homeworks/docs/