{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,150p' /Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/AudioExplainer/README.md; sed -n '45,130p' /Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/AudioExplainer/src/audioexplainer/engine.py; rg -n -i \\\"budget constraint|indifference curve\\\" /Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/econ100a-slides_homeworks/docs/S2* /Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/intermediate_micro_notes -g '*.md' -g '*.tex' | sed -n '1,180p'; sed -n '1,165p' /Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/InteractiveEduHub/main/models.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,150p' /Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/AudioExplainer/README.md; sed -n '45,130p' /Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/AudioExplainer/src/audioexplainer/engine.py; rg -n -i \\\"budget constraint|indifference curve\\\" /Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/econ100a-slides_homeworks/docs/S2* /Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/intermediate_micro_notes -g '*.md' -g '*.tex' | sed -n '1,180p'; sed -n '1,165p' /Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/InteractiveEduHub/main/models.py\"","aggregated_output":"# AudioExplainer\n\nAudioExplainer turns a prepared script into a neural-voice MP3, a Markdown\ntranscript, and a dependency-free browser player. It is designed for AI agents,\ndeveloper tools, and command-line workflows that already have the context needed\nto write the explanation.\n\nThe host application writes the script. AudioExplainer only preprocesses and\nsynthesizes it; it does not call a language model.\n\n> **Project status:** alpha. Interfaces and generated metadata may change before\n> a stable release.\n\n## Features\n\n- Spanish and English monologues or two-speaker dialogue\n- online neural speech through `edge-tts`\n- optional local neural fallback through Piper\n- local system-voice fallback on macOS\n- automatic provider fallback: Edge → Piper → system voice\n- Markdown-aware narration, including headings, emphasis, and formulas\n- synchronized transcript for every provider: exact Edge boundaries when\n  available and clearly labelled duration-based alignment for local voices\n- accessible local player with seeking, transcript following, and playback speed\n  adjustments in 0.05x steps\n- per-directory audio library and versioned metadata sidecars\n\n## Install\n\nInstall the standard package:\n\n```bash\nuv tool install .\n```\n\nTo add the local neural fallback:\n\n```bash\nuv tool install '.[piper]'\naudioexplain --setup-piper\n```\n\nAudio conversion and duration detection require `ffmpeg` and `ffprobe`. Run the\nhealth check after installation:\n\n```bash\naudioexplain --doctor\n```\n\nPiper is an optional, separately distributed GPL-licensed runtime. Downloaded\nvoice models retain their own licenses.\n\n## Use\n\nCreate a Spanish monologue from standard input:\n\n```bash\nprintf '%s' \"Aquí tienes un resumen breve del cambio.\" | \\\n  audioexplain --title \"resumen\" --out-dir deliverables\n```\n\nRead a Markdown file in English:\n\n```bash\naudioexplain --input script.md --english \\\n  --title \"daily recap\" --out-dir deliverables\n```\n\nCreate a two-voice explanation from `Host:` and `Guest:` lines:\n\n```bash\naudioexplain --style dialogue --input dialogue.md \\\n  --title \"deep dive\" --out-dir deliverables\n```\n\nKeep synthesis local with Piper:\n\n```bash\naudioexplain --provider piper --input private-notes.md\n```\n\nEach run prints the absolute MP3 path and writes the transcript, player, and\nmetadata next to it. The default output directory is temporary; pass an explicit\n`--out-dir` when the artifacts should persist.\n\n## Browser player\n\nThe generated `.player.html` works without a server or external assets. It\nincludes:\n\n- play/pause and primary `-10` / `+10` second controls\n- optional precise jumps of `-15`, `-5`, `+5`, and `+15` seconds\n- a progress scrubber and elapsed/total time\n- compact `− / speed / +` controls from 0.75x to 2x in exact 0.05x steps\n- an article view and sentence-level view\n- Markdown rendering and formula presentation\n- current-sentence highlighting and optional automatic scrolling\n\nEdge supplies exact sentence events when available. If those events are missing\nor invalid, and for Piper and the macOS system voice which do not provide them,\nAudioExplainer distributes the measured audio duration across sentences and\nlabels their tracking as approximate.\n\nIf a browser surface blocks local `file://` pages, serve the output directory:\n\n```bash\ncd deliverables\npython3 -m http.server 8765 --bind 127.0.0.1\n```\n\nThen open `http://127.0.0.1:8765/<file>.player.html`.\n\n## Providers and privacy\n\nFor ordinary text, `--provider auto` tries Edge neural speech first, then local\nPiper, then the macOS system voice. If the safety check detects an obvious\ncredential, automatic mode skips the online provider. Edge synthesis is an\nonline service and sends narration text to Microsoft. `edge-tts` is an\nindependent client and is not an official Azure Speech SDK; service availability\ncan change.\n\nUse `--provider piper` or `--provider say` for material that must remain local.\nAudioExplainer refuses obvious credentials with the online provider unless\n`--allow-sensitive` is supplied explicitly.\n\n## Agent discovery templates\n\nReusable discovery snippets live in `share/templates/discovery/`. They teach a\nhost agent to write an audio-first script, call `audioexplain`, and return the\nabsolute output paths. Review and copy a template into the relevant agent's\nconfiguration only when you want that integration.\n\n## Development\n\n```bash\nuv sync --extra dev\nuv run pytest\nuv build\n```\n\nSee [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) for contribution guidance and\n[SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md) for private vulnerability reporting.\n\n## License\n\nMIT. See [LICENSE](LICENSE).\nSAMPLE_RATE = 24000\nMP3_BITRATE = \"64k\"\nPARAGRAPH_PAUSE_MS = 300\nDIALOGUE_PAUSE_MS = 400\n_MIN_AUDIO_BYTES = 800\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass TimedSegment:\n    \"\"\"One spoken sentence on the final media timeline, in seconds.\"\"\"\n\n    text: str\n    start_s: float\n    end_s: float\n    part_index: int\n    speaker: str | None = None\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass SyncTrack:\n    \"\"\"Provider-neutral sentence timing suitable for a media player or sidecar.\"\"\"\n\n    segments: tuple[TimedSegment, ...]\n    granularity: str = \"sentence\"\n    source: str = \"unknown\"\n    timebase: str = \"media_seconds\"\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass SynthResult:\n    audio_path: Path\n    transcript_path: Path\n    provider: str\n    provider_reason: str\n    duration_s: float | None\n    n_parts: int\n    # Defaults preserve the original positional six-field construction API.\n    sync: SyncTrack | None = None\n    formulas: tuple[object, ...] = ()\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass _SpeechPart:\n    \"\"\"Internal input to one provider request; speaker is not part of cue text.\"\"\"\n\n    voice: str\n    text: str\n    speaker: str | None = None\n\n    def __iter__(self) -> Iterator[str]:\n        \"\"\"Keep legacy two-item unpacking used by engine test doubles working.\"\"\"\n        yield self.voice\n        yield self.text\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass _PreparedContent:\n    spoken_text: str\n    formulas: tuple[object, ...] = ()\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n# Provider selection (D1 = auto)\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #\ndef _network_ok(host: str = _EDGE_PROBE_HOST, port: int = 443, timeout: float = 2.0) -> bool:\n    try:\n        socket.create_connection((host, port), timeout=timeout).close()\n        return True\n    except OSError:\n        return False\n\n\ndef choose_provider(provider: str, text: str):\n    \"\"\"Return (provider_obj, reason). Implements the D1 auto policy.\"\"\"\n    edge, piper, say = EdgeProvider(), PiperProvider(), SayProvider()\n    if provider == \"edge\":\n        if not edge.available():\n            raise ProviderError(\"--provider edge requested but edge-tts is not installed\")\n        return edge, \"edge (explicit)\"\n    if provider == \"piper\":\n        if not piper.available():\n            raise ProviderError(\n                \"--provider piper requested but its local neural voice is not ready; \"\n                \"run `audioexplain --setup-piper`\"\n            )\n        return piper, \"piper (explicit, local neural)\"\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/econ100a-slides_homeworks/docs/S2_Budget_Constraint_Ch2.md:3:## Budget Constraint\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/econ100a-slides_homeworks/docs/S2_Budget_Constraint_Ch2.md:36:## Affordable Bundles - Budget Constraints\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/econ100a-slides_homeworks/docs/S2_Budget_Constraint_Ch2.md:47:## Affordable Bundles - Budget Constraints\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/econ100a-slides_homeworks/docs/S2_Budget_Constraint_Ch2.md:57:## \"Budget line\" or \"budget constraint\"\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/econ100a-slides_homeworks/docs/S2_Budget_Constraint_Ch2.md:60:conform the consumer’s **budget constraint** or **budget line**.\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/econ100a-slides_homeworks/docs/S2_Budget_Constraint_Ch2.md:77:* Notice that the _budget constraint_ (or _budget line_) is the upper boundary of the _budget set_.\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/econ100a-slides_homeworks/docs/S2_Budget_Constraint_Ch2.md:134:* The budget constraint and budget set depend upon prices and income. What happens as prices or income change?\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/econ100a-slides_homeworks/docs/S2_Budget_Constraint_Ch2.md:185:* Budget constraint pivots: slope get steeper from $ -p_1 / p_2 $ to $ -p_1'/p_2 $\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/econ100a-slides_homeworks/docs/S2_Budget_Constraint_Ch2.md:235:* How does a food stamp alter a family’s budget constraint?\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/econ100a-slides_homeworks/docs/S2_Budget_Constraint_Ch2.md:239:* The budget constraint is then $ F + G = 400 $\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/econ100a-slides_homeworks/docs/S2_Budget_Constraint_Ch2.html:50:<h2>Budget Constraint</h2>\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/econ100a-slides_homeworks/docs/S2_Budget_Constraint_Ch2.html:74:<h2>Affordable Bundles - Budget Constraints</h2>\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/econ100a-slides_homeworks/docs/S2_Budget_Constraint_Ch2.html:85:<h2>Affordable Bundles - Budget Constraints</h2>\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/econ100a-slides_homeworks/docs/S2_Budget_Constraint_Ch2.html:95:<h2>“Budget line” or “budget constraint”</h2>\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/econ100a-slides_homeworks/docs/S2_Budget_Constraint_Ch2.html:97:<li><p>The set of bundles that are <strong>just affordable</strong> in that they exhaust the consumer’s income, conform the consumer’s <strong>budget constraint</strong> or <strong>budget line</strong>.</p></li>\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/econ100a-slides_homeworks/docs/S2_Budget_Constraint_Ch2.html:112:<li>Notice that the <em>budget constraint</em> (or <em>budget line</em>) is the upper boundary of the <em>budget set</em>.</li>\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/econ100a-slides_homeworks/docs/S2_Budget_Constraint_Ch2.html:153:<li><p>The budget constraint and budget set depend upon prices and income. What happens as prices or income change?</p></li>\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/econ100a-slides_homeworks/docs/S2_Budget_Constraint_Ch2.html:184:<li><p>Budget constraint pivots: slope get steeper from $ -p_1 / p_2 $ to $ -p_1’/p_2 $</p></li>\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/econ100a-slides_homeworks/docs/S2_Budget_Constraint_Ch2.html:221:<li><p>How does a food stamp alter a family’s budget constraint?</p></li>\n/Users/klopezva/GithubRepos/econ100a-slides_homeworks/docs/S2_Budget_Constraint_Ch2.html:223:<li><p>The budget constraint is then $ F + G = 400 $</p></li>\nfrom django.contrib.auth.models import AbstractUser\nfrom django.db import models\nimport uuid\nfrom django.contrib.auth.hashers import make_password\nclass CustomUser(AbstractUser):\n    # Definir opciones para el campo 'role'\n    ROLE_CHOICES = (\n        ('instructor', 'Instructor'),\n        ('student', 'Student'),\n        ('teaching_assistant', 'Teaching Assistant'),\n        ('admin','administrator'),\n        # Agregar otros roles si es necesario\n    )\n    \n    preferred_language = models.CharField(\n        max_length=10,\n        choices=[('en', 'English'), ('es', 'Espanol')],\n        default='en'  # Idioma por defecto\n    )\n\n    # Campos adicionales para el usuario\n    name = models.CharField(max_length=50)\n    lastname = models.CharField(max_length=50)\n    middlename = models.CharField(max_length=50)\n    ucsc_id = models.CharField(max_length=20, unique=False)\n    affiliation = models.CharField(max_length=100, default='')\n    # Campo 'role' para almacenar el rol del usuario\n    role = models.CharField(max_length=20, choices=ROLE_CHOICES)\n    def set_password(self, raw_password):\n        from django.contrib.auth.hashers import make_password\n        \"\"\"\n        Sobrescribe el método set_password para hashear la contraseña\n        utilizando el algoritmo de hash deseado.\n        \"\"\"\n        self.password = make_password(raw_password)    \n\n    def __str__(self):\n        return self.username  # Representación en string del usuario\n\n#model for course\nclass CoursesContents(models.Model):\n    custom_id = models.CharField(max_length=36, unique=True, default=uuid.uuid4, editable=False)\n    author = models.ForeignKey(CustomUser, on_delete=models.CASCADE)\n    directory_name = models.CharField(max_length=100)\n    display_name = models.CharField(max_length=100)\n\n    def __str__(self):\n        return self.display_name\n    \n\n\nclass Subject(models.Model):\n    #custom_id = models.CharField(max_length=36)\n    custom_id = models.CharField(max_length=36, unique=True, default=uuid.uuid4, editable=False)\n    name = models.CharField(max_length=100)\n    instructor = models.ForeignKey(CustomUser, on_delete=models.CASCADE, null=True, blank=True, limit_choices_to={'role': 'instructor'}, related_name='taught_subjects')\n    teaching_assistant = models.ManyToManyField(CustomUser, blank=True, limit_choices_to={'role': 'teaching_assistant', 'ucsc_id__isnull': False}, related_name='assisted_subjects')\n    #teaching_assistant = models.ManyToManyField(CustomUser, on_delete=models.CASCADE, blank=True, limit_choices_to={'role': 'teaching_assistant', 'ucsc_id__isnull': False}, related_name='assisted_subjects')\n    #teaching_assistant = models.ManyToManyField(CustomUser, on_delete=models.CASCADE, null=True, blank=True, limit_choices_to={'role': 'teaching_assistant', 'ucsc_id__isnull': False}, related_name='assisted_subjects')\n    title = models.CharField(max_length=100)\n    topic = models.CharField(max_length=100)\n    university = models.CharField(max_length=100)\n    term = models.CharField(max_length=100)\n    course_content = models.ForeignKey(CoursesContents, on_delete=models.CASCADE, related_name='subjects', null=True, blank=True)\n    \n\nclass Inscription(models.Model):\n    student = models.ForeignKey(CustomUser, on_delete=models.CASCADE, limit_choices_to={'role': 'student'})\n    subject = models.ForeignKey(Subject, on_delete=models.CASCADE)\n    inscription_date = models.DateField(auto_now_add=True)\n    state = models.CharField(max_length=50, default='Pendant')\n\nclass Responses(models.Model):\n    student = models.OneToOneField(CustomUser, on_delete=models.CASCADE, limit_choices_to={'role': 'student'})\n    subject = models.CharField(max_length=100)  # Nombre de la clase\n    module_name = models.CharField(max_length=100)\n    submodule_name1 = models.CharField(max_length=100)\n    submodule_name2 = models.CharField(max_length=100)\n    question_number = models.IntegerField()\n    response = models.CharField(max_length=100)\n    is_correct = models.BooleanField()  \n    response_time = models.DateTimeField(auto_now_add=True)\n\n\nclass PageVisit(models.Model):\n    username = models.CharField(max_length=50)\n    subject_name = models.CharField(max_length=50)\n    subject_custom_id = models.CharField(max_length=50)\n    page = models.CharField(max_length=100)\n    number_of_visits = models.IntegerField(default=0)\n    total_time = models.DurationField(default=0)\n    total_time_in_seconds = models.IntegerField(default=0)\n        \nclass StudentResponses(models.Model):\n    username = models.CharField(max_length=50)\n    course_name = models.CharField(max_length=50)\n    subject_custom_id = models.CharField(max_length=50)\n    class_name = models.CharField(max_length=50)\n    page_path = models.CharField(max_length=100)\n    type_of_question = models.CharField(max_length=100)\n    question_number = models.IntegerField(default=0)\n    response = models.CharField(max_length=100)\n    is_correct = models.CharField(max_length=100)\n    response_time = models.DateTimeField(auto_now_add=True)\n    response_dict = models.JSONField(default=dict)  \n    \n    '''\n    response_dict = {\n            'page_path': current_url,\n            'type_of_question': type_of_question,\n            'question_number': numero_de_pregunta,\n            'response': respuesta,\n            'is_correct': es_respuesta_correcta,\n            'response_time': response_time_str,\n        }\n    '''\n        \n\nclass StudentCompleteness(models.Model):\n    \"\"\"\n    Store status of answered questions and page completion for a student.\n\n    Example structure of `student_progress_dict`:\n    {\n        'IntermediateMicro_main/modules/module2/budget_restriction/questions.html': {\n            'type_of_question': 'Static Question',\n            'questions': {\n                '1': {'completed_question': 'yes'},\n                '2': {'completed_question': 'not'}\n            },\n            'completed_page': 'yes'\n        },\n        'IntermediateMicro_main/modules/module3/elasticity/questions.html': {\n            'type_of_question': 'Interactive Question',\n            'questions': {\n                '1': {'completed_question': 'yes'}\n            },\n            'completed_page': 'not'\n        }\n    }\n    \"\"\"\n    username = models.CharField(max_length=50)\n    subject_custom_id = models.CharField(max_length=50)\n    student_progress_dict = models.JSONField(default=dict)","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
